                                "sense_id": "1f651ec5-880f-34a3-9f9c-25edb09e2864",
                                "text": "And outside was the garden, with its lemon-trees growing in vast jars-like the jars of Knossos—but marked with Barberini bees; its white and red camellias becarpeting the soft grass with their fallen petals; […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "476afb10-d059-4c47-9293-5d4b0331a388",
                                "sense_id": "1f651ec5-880f-34a3-9f9c-25edb09e2864",
                                "text": "The billet-village decks its glades / With leafy poplar-colonnades / And apple-orchards where the bloom / Makes every tree a great mushroom / Of petals pink as summer dawn, / Soon to becarpet all the lawn […]"
